  "raw_text": "215\n\nSibrin lâka\n \n(a/t:\n \nSibraia lâka\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfear, fearfulness\n \n/ miedo, espanto\n\n(Construct:\n \nSibrinki l\nâ\nka, Sibrinkam l\nâ\nka, Sibrinka l\nâ\nka\n)\n\nSibrin lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto feel fear, to feel afraid\n \n/ sentir miedo\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\ndb-Param Marikan 14:7\n):\n \nMan nani bui Gâd ra sibrin luks\n \n–\n \n(You) feel fear of God\n \n/ (Ustedes)\nsientan temor de Dios)\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nwqu-11/19\n):\n \nSins Lâka 29:25 aisi ba tânka ra, ¿dîa muni yawan upla ra sibrin lukaia apia sa ki?\n \n–\n\nAccording to Proverbs 29:25, why must we not feel afraid of people?\n \n/ Según Proverbios 29:25, ¿por qué\nno debemos tener miedo de las personas?)\n\nSibrin pura luaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto overcome fear\n \n/ superar el miedo\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n06/20\n):\n \nJehova hilpka wal Moses ba ai sibrinka nani pura luan\n \n–\n \nWith Jehovah’s help, Moses\n\novercame his fears\n \n/ Con la ayuda de Jehová, Moisés superó sus temores\n)\n\nSibripara\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nSi bripara\n) (v\n-\nproh)\n \n–\n \ndo not be afraid\n \n/ no tengas miedo\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nLuk\n \n1:30\n):\n \nSi bripara, Meri\n \n–\n \nDo not\n \nbe afraid\n,\n \nMary\n \n/ No tengas miedo\n,\n \nMar\ní\na)\n\nUpla ra sibriaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto fear man\n \n/ temer al hombre\n\nUpla ra sibrin briaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto have fear of man\n \n/ tener miedo al hombre\n\nUpla ra sibrin briaia ba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nthe having of the fear of man\n \n/ el tener miedo al hombre\n\nSîa\n \n(adv)\n \n–\n \nfor fear of, in order not to\n \n/ por miedo a, para no\n\nSîa plapaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto run in fear\n \n/ correr por miedo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh66\n):\n \nWaihlam kum sia plapisma,...\n \n–\n \nYou run in fear of your enemy,...\n \n/ Corres por miedo a tu enemigo, ...)\n\nSîa\n \nyabaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto give in to fear of, to fear, to be afraid of, to detest, to be disgusted\n \n/ ceder al miedo,\ntemer, tener miedo, detestar, estar asqueado\n \n(Alt:\n \nSîa yaia\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nUpla nani ra sia yapara\n \n–\n \nDo not give in to the fear of people\n \n/ No cedas al miedo a las personas.)\n\nSîa yabi kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be in fear, to have given in to fear\n \n/ estar asustado, haber cedido al miedo\n\nSiahka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \na cold\n \n(not referring to temperature, but the sickness) / un resfriado (no se refiere a la temperatura, sino\na la enfermedad)\n\nSiahka alkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto catch a cold\n \n/ resfriarse\n\nSiahka ai alkan\n \n–\n \nI caught a cold\n \n/ tengo un resfriado\n\nSiahka mai alkan\n \n–\n \nyou caught a cold\n \n/ tienes un resfriado\n\nSiahka briaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto have a cold\n \n/ estar resfriado\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nWitin siahka brisa\n \n–\n \nHe has a cold\n \n/ Él está resfriado\n)\n\nSiahka kuhbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cough because of a cold\n \n/ toser por un resfriado\n\nSiakwa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsmall freshwater turtle\n \n/\n \ntortuga pequena de\n \nagua dulce\n\nSiakwa kati\n \n–\n \nJanuary\n \n/ enero\n\n(Lit:\n \nsmall turtle moon\n \n/ luna de la tortuga pequeña\n)\n\nSibin\n \n(\ngpm\n-from English / de inglés) (Formerly/Anteriormente:\n \nMatlalkahbi pura kum\n)\n \n–\n \nseven\n \n/ siete\n\nSibrin\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nSi,\n \nSibriaia\n\nSig\narit\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nSigaret, Sikarit\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncigarette\n,\n \ncigar\n \n/ cigarrillo\n,\n \ncigarro\n\nSigarit diaia\n \n(\nypq,lv,bh,km,mwb\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto smoke cigarettes\n \n/ fumar cigarrillos\n\nSika\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nSi\n \n(1)\n\nSîka\n \n(sika)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmedicine\n, remedy, drug,\n \nbait\n \n/ medicina, remedio, droga, cebo\n \n(usado pa\nra pescar)\n\n(Construct:\n \nSaika\n/\nSaîka\n)\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \ndict,dictu\n \ngive\n \n“\nworm\n”\n \nas a definition but that is only correct if it is referring to bait for fishing.\n \nLiwa\n \nis the word for\n\n“\nworm\n”\n.\n \n/\n \ndict\n,\n \ndictu\n \nda al\n \n“\ngusano\n”\n \ncomo definición, pero eso solo es correcto si se refiere al cebo para la pesca.\n \nLiwa\n \nes la\n\npalabra para\n \n“\ngusano\n”\n.\n)\n\nSîka daka\nka\nia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto give medicine\n \n/ dar medicina\n\nSîka diaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto take medicine, to drink medicine\n \n/ tomar medicina\n\nSîka m\nâ\nka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nincense, myrrh, sacrificial smoke\n \n/ incienso, mirra, humo de sacrificio\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb\n):\n \nsîka maka kîa painkira\n \n–\n \nperfumed incense\n \n/ incienso perfumado)\n\nSikbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto clean, to wash, to rinse\n \n/ limpiar, lavar, enjuagar\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nJisas apastil nani mina ba sikban\n \n–\n \nJesus washed\n \nhis apostles feet\n \n/ Jesús lavó los pies de sus apóstoles\n)\n\nMihta sikbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto wash hands\n \n/ lavarse las manos\n\nSikbi sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto wash away, to rinse away, to rinse off\n \n/ lavar, enjuagar\n\nSikia\n \n(\nbc,dict,dictu\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \navocado\n \n/ aguacate",
